WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.700
So President Joe Biden had his meeting with
Republicans at the White House on Monday night

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:06.930
to talk about the covid relief bill.

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:11.790
Joe Biden had proposed a one point nine dollars
billion package.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:17.640
Republicans were allowed to express to Joe
Biden why they want a six hundred and eighteen

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:18.890
dollars billion package.

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:23.850
But it's now being made abundantly clear that
Joe Biden and Democrats are hopefully ready

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.520
to move ahead without Republicans.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:30.130
That's what Joe Biden's press secretary, Jen
Psaki, said earlier this week at a White House

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:31.369
press briefing.

00:00:31.369 --> 00:00:34.320
It's what Joe Biden seems to be communicating.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.680
And I hope that it's time to just go and do
it, because at this point in time, I don't

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:41.989
see the benefit to anybody in the Democratic
Party.

00:00:41.989 --> 00:00:46.719
And that includes Joe Biden as well as Democrats
in the House and Senate of waiting with the

00:00:46.719 --> 00:00:53.329
idea that maybe some Republicans might be
OK with some kind of completely flaccid and

00:00:53.329 --> 00:00:59.110
pathetic compromise between the one point
nine trillion and the six hundred and eighteen

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:00.110
billion.

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:06.929
And at this point, the perspective should
be if Republicans realize that the one point

00:01:06.929 --> 00:01:13.869
nine dollars billion package and what it contains
is popular even with some of their constituents,

00:01:13.869 --> 00:01:17.630
it's Republican voters who want the stimulus
package, too.

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:22.329
If some Republicans realize that, then maybe
they'll vote for it in the House or vote for

00:01:22.329 --> 00:01:27.579
it in the Senate if they don't realize that
or realize it but don't care.

00:01:27.579 --> 00:01:31.590
And every single Republican decides to vote
against the one point nine dollars billion

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:35.139
covid stimulus package, let them do it at
their own peril.

00:01:35.139 --> 00:01:43.289
And what I mean by that is once their names
are on the record as saying, no, I'm against

00:01:43.289 --> 00:01:49.209
the covid stimulus package that is popular
even with many of my Republican constituents,

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:54.109
well, then it'll be up to Republican voters
to decide whether they want to reelect those

00:01:54.109 --> 00:01:55.729
very same Republicans.

00:01:55.729 --> 00:02:00.709
And my guess is you will get some Republicans
to come along with Joe Biden's plan because

00:02:00.709 --> 00:02:03.950
they realize that many of their constituents
want it.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:09.099
So Joe Biden has been widely criticized for
sitting down with Republicans on Monday night

00:02:09.099 --> 00:02:11.250
and not with Democrats.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:14.599
Some hot take saying this is a right wing
president.

00:02:14.599 --> 00:02:16.829
He talks to Republicans, but not Democrats.

00:02:16.829 --> 00:02:19.600
I think that that is very far from what is
going on.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:25.700
I am pleased, increasingly that Joe Biden
and Democrats aren't budging on the one point

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:27.790
nine dollars billion proposal.

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:32.700
Joe Biden had no need to meet with Democrats
because Joe Biden and Democrats mostly are

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:36.840
on the same page about the one point nine
trillion dollar stimulus package.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:41.130
Do the meeting with Republicans because Joe
Biden said that he wanted unity.

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:42.900
He said he wanted bipartisanship.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:47.010
He said he would work with Republicans and
he's trying to add that olive branch was this

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:48.330
meeting on Monday night.

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:49.860
But it's time to stop.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:55.930
When Joe Biden said if we win these Georgia
races, two thousand dollar checks go out immediately.

00:02:55.930 --> 00:03:01.150
That doesn't mean you negotiate with bad faith
actor Republicans into March and hopefully

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:04.200
get checks out by the end of March, if not
early April.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:05.660
Enough time has gone by.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:10.129
And if Joe Biden and Democrats don't move
forward on the one point nine trillion, put

00:03:10.129 --> 00:03:11.129
it at risk.

00:03:11.129 --> 00:03:14.060
You know, if Republicans really want to vote
against that, let them do it.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:17.420
But if Joe Biden doesn't move forward with
this, it is going to be a failure.

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:23.959
In Joe Biden's column, he was very clear about
what he would do and what it would mean to

00:03:23.959 --> 00:03:29.329
add Senate control for Democrats in addition
to Joe Biden taking the White House from Donald

00:03:29.329 --> 00:03:30.469
Trump.

00:03:30.469 --> 00:03:34.139
And we will now see if they are going to put
their money where their mouths are.

00:03:34.139 --> 00:03:40.709
Now, I think that the calculation to be made,
there's a couple of calculations here.

00:03:40.709 --> 00:03:46.379
When you think about this from a political
strategy standpoint, Democrats, by not budging

00:03:46.379 --> 00:03:49.920
on one point nine trillion, are doing a couple
of different things.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:56.540
Number one, I hope Democrats and Joe Biden
realize that if you meet somewhere in the

00:03:56.540 --> 00:04:00.379
middle, like, imagine that Democrats say,
OK, you know what, we want one point nine

00:04:00.379 --> 00:04:01.709
trillion.

00:04:01.709 --> 00:04:04.330
Republicans want six hundred and eighteen
billion.

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:07.790
Let's do one point three trillion or something
like that.

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:13.730
A ton of Republicans are still going to vote
against it, even though it will end up likely

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:14.730
passing.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:20.359
And so Republicans will end up getting the
benefit of it, passing and money getting to

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:26.150
their constituents while continuing to be
able to vertue signal about the debt and the

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:28.780
deficit and spending and what not.

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:32.160
Everybody deserves the money and all of this
sort of stuff.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:38.780
So the calculation I hope Democrats are making
is they know the plan is more popular with

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:42.900
the country than the portion of people who
voted for Joe Biden.

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:46.860
In other words, this is a covid stimulus package
that's popular with 60, 65, 70 percent of

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:48.460
the country.

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:50.520
That's much more than the share that voted
for Joe Biden.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:55.021
That means there are millions of Republican
voters that like this plan and they want it

00:04:55.021 --> 00:04:56.150
to pass.

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:59.470
If Democrats realize that and they realize
even if.

00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:04.850
We negotiate with Republicans, many of them
will still vote against it, let's just move

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:05.850
forward.

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:09.889
We have the ability to do this via budget
reconciliation, assuming all 50 Democrats

00:05:09.889 --> 00:05:14.789
in the Senate are on board, which is still
a bit of a question mark, but is likely.

00:05:14.789 --> 00:05:19.560
Let's actually put these Republican senators
in particular and members of the House in

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:23.360
a position of having to vote against something
that their constituents want.

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:25.120
Let them vote no.

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:26.680
Let them say it's bad.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:30.660
Let them then have to go and explain their
votes to their constituents.

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:35.759
I believe this is a political risk very much
worth taking for Joe Biden and Democrats.

00:05:35.759 --> 00:05:39.479
I think the meeting was a fine move for Joe
Biden.

00:05:39.479 --> 00:05:43.940
He's giving the Republicans an opportunity
to show they actually want to help the American

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:44.940
people.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:52.900
They present a counter offer that's so pathetic
and pitiful that it's humiliating and embarrassing

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:57.949
and now put them in the position of actually
saying, are you really going to vote for nothing

00:05:57.949 --> 00:05:59.430
for your constituents?

00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:02.830
Are you going to try to prevent any money
from going out?

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:04.360
Because this is the package.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:07.050
So I'm fine with the meeting.

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:09.000
I'm fine with not budging.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:11.440
I'm fine with moving forward without Republicans.

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:17.000
The question now is, can Joe Biden actually
get it done if he can get it done, his early

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:21.099
approval on covid and in general is going
to persist.

00:06:21.099 --> 00:06:27.250
It's going to be booted for lack of a better
term if Joe Biden fails to get this done or

00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:28.720
something close to it.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:33.379
Like I think even if Joe Biden did 600 billion
in the end, I think it would be considered

00:06:33.379 --> 00:06:34.379
a failure.

00:06:34.379 --> 00:06:35.970
He said two thousand dollar checks are going
out now.

00:06:35.970 --> 00:06:40.849
We're already talking about adding fourteen
hundred to the six hundred to make it a total

00:06:40.849 --> 00:06:41.849
of two thousand.

00:06:41.849 --> 00:06:44.169
That's already a concession that I don't like
to see.

00:06:44.169 --> 00:06:48.600
If Biden can't get this done and get it done
the next 10 to 14 days, it is going to be

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:50.849
the first major failure of the Biden administration.

00:06:50.849 --> 00:06:53.000
Let's hope it doesn't happen.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:56.330
I remain cautiously optimistic that it will
get done.

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:59.659
I like the way Democrats are just saying it's
one point nine trillion.

00:06:59.659 --> 00:07:00.920
That's what it is.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:01.920
Vote no.

00:07:01.920 --> 00:08:23.909
If you want Republicans, I think many will
end up voting for it

